Jove wrote:

> (Tip: #adjust your largest dagger stack to 'Q', requivering
> is then just 'QQ'.  If you have autoquiver on, adjust any
> other stacks to the sequence "RST...", as autoquiver looks
> for quiverable items in a-zA-Z order.  #adjust rocks to 't'
> so they can be thrown by hitting 'tt')

Here's another tip. If you don't have autopickup on for weapons, try 
adding this line to your defaults.nh file:
autopickup_exception="<*<A>"

Now you can name your daggers (or any other object) <A> and you'll pick 
them up automatically. Of course you could come up with your own tag, I 
just picked <A> for auto.

>   - If you don't mean to wield one of your stack of enchanted
>     daggers, you'll have to decide whether to enchant your wielded
>     weapon before your dagger stack.

And in case you hadn't figured this out, if you do want to wield one of 
the stack, name the lot (see above), drop all but one, re-name that 
something else and pick the others up. Now the one stays seperate so you 
can wield it still have the others quivered (plus you won't accidently 
throw your melee weapon). To re-stack the wielded dagger (eg. for more 
enchanting) unname it (at the name prompt type a space), drop it and 
pick it up again.

